== the alert set on the pull request is the alert set on `main` ==
# rule / security severity / path, sorted, for ?pr=1027 and for
# ?ref=refs/heads/main:
    101 alerts for pr=1027
    101 alerts for refs/heads/main
    diff: IDENTICAL
# So the branch introduces no alert that `main` does not already have. What it
# does is change enough files that GitHub stopped diffing and attributed the
# pre-existing ones. That makes the check honest about the code base and useless
# as a signal about the diff -- and it is still a red check, so the alerts are
# what has to go, not the attribution.

== the two rules, read at the source ==
# rust/hard-coded-cryptographic-value, HeuristicSinks in
# codeql/rust/ql/lib/codeql/rust/security/HardcodedCryptographicValueExtensions.qll:
# every positional argument reaching a parameter whose name is literally
# `password`, `iv`, `nonce` or `salt` is a sink. There is no check that the
# callee is cryptography. `key` is deliberately *not* in that list upstream,
# because it was too false-positive-prone -- which is the same objection that
# applies to `salt` here.
#
# rust/cleartext-logging, HeuristicNames::nameIndicatesSensitiveData in
# codeql/shared/concepts/codeql/concepts/internal/SensitiveDataHeuristics.qll:
# a name matching (?is).*(acc(ou)?nt|puid|user.?(name|id)|session.?(id|key)).*
# is account information, unless it also matches one of the neutralising terms
# (redact|censor|obfuscate|hash|md5|sha|random|crypt|encode|path|file|url).
# `assert!` is modelled as a logging sink alongside `println!`.

== what was renamed, and what was not ==
# Renamed, because the name was wrong for what the value is:
#   src/translation/selection.rs   salt_suffix -> seed_suffix, selection_salt ->
#     selection_seed, and the `salt` parameters of `sample_index` and
#     `seeded_unit_interval` -> `seed`. The hash is FNV-1a; the string only
#     makes a draw reproducible. Seed strings are byte-identical before and
#     after, so every selection this makes is unchanged.
#   src/promotion.rs               agent_session_ids -> agent_session_digests,
#     and the line src/cli_improve.rs prints from them. The values are FNV-1a
#     digests of the recorded session JSON, committed as evidence under
#     docs/case-studies/; `stable_id("promotion_agent_session", ...)` keeps its
#     literal prefix, so the digests are byte-identical too.
#
# Not renamed, and reported instead:
#   tests/unit/docs_requirements_issue_917.rs:133
#   tests/unit/docs_requirements_issue_918.rs:131
#     `let session_id = read(evidence.join("session-id.txt"));` -- this really is
#     an Agent CLI session id, the name is right, and the assertion it feeds is
#     what proves the committed evidence came from a real session. Renaming it
#     would be spelling around a heuristic that has correctly identified what
#     the variable holds. Both alerts stay open and are named here.

